00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:44.830
First up is an extended scene at the shopping
mall which Simon Kinberg has described as

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:48.720
an 80s montage, set to music and with some
interesting easter eggs.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.469
The movie's production team located an unused
period mall in Montreal and got permission

00:00:53.469 --> 00:00:57.469
to renovate it, fitting it out with retail
outlets and brands you'd expect to see in

00:00:57.469 --> 00:00:59.260
a typical 80s American mall.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:03.859
A video arcade in the mall was refurbished
with vintage machines and rebranded as Space

00:01:03.859 --> 00:01:08.540
Port, which was the name of the video arcade
where director Bryan Singer played as a kid.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:13.130
The mall scene culminates in Cyclops, Jean
Grey, Jubilee and Nightcrawler coming out

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:15.650
of a movie theatre after watching Return of
the Jedi.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:20.941
That final part is included in the theatrical
release but the rest was cut as, according

00:01:20.941 --> 00:01:25.729
to the filmmakers, it slowed down the movie
too much.

00:01:25.729 --> 00:01:29.650
Sophie Turner teased another part of the mall
sequence when she posted a picture of herself

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:32.240
as Jean Grey shopping at the mall with Cyclops.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:37.060
It's a very cool easter egg to the comic book
mutant Dazzler who first appeared in the X-Men

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:42.770
comics in 1980 and who has the power to transform
sound waves into light beams and energy.

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:47.369
The album "Dazzler: Sounds of Light and Fury"
that Scott Summers is holding actually appears

00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:50.659
on the cover of issue 29 of the comic book
Dazzler.

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:54.259
And there's another amusing moment in the
record store when Scott picks up an album

00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:59.530
featuring Boy George and asks Jean, has "anyone
ever told you, you look like this?!"

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:04.500
Although Jubilee's role was cut down in the
final film, they did shoot an important scene

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.869
at the shopping mall where she got to use
her powers.

00:02:06.869 --> 00:02:12.250
In the comics, Jubilee has the power to produce
explosive balls of energy-plasma or fireworks.

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:16.290
By the way, the shopping mall itself is an
easter egg to how Jubilee discovered her powers

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:21.010
in the comics after running away from a mall
security guard, and it's also where she met

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:24.570
other X-Men members including Storm, Rogue,
Psylocke and Dazzler.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:29.890
It's rumoured that the deleted scene is similar
to the comics, with Jubilee using her powers

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:35.970
and then having to escape from the mall's
security using her gymnastic abilities.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:39.940
Nightcrawler also had some amusing scenes
at the mall, including a moment when he starts

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.140
breakdancing with a group of kids.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:45.680
And in another funny scene, the four mutants
are drinking cold drinks when Nightcrawler

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.830
becomes scared as he gets an ice-cream headache.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:53.070
But when Scott tells him not to worry, it's
a just brain freeze, Nightcrawler gets even

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:57.080
more frightened as he thinks his brain is
about to freeze over!

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:02.990
Also hidden in the mall sequence is an homage
to the 1980s movie Moscow on the Hudson starring

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:03.990
Robin Williams.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:08.610
As the young mutants walk around, Nightcrawler
who is new to America, is amazed that ordinary

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.500
people don't fear them as mutants.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:14.590
Nightcrawler thinks "the mall is [a] paradise"
and it parallels how Robin Williams' Russian

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:18.880
character feels when he arrives in America
in Moscow on the Hudson.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:23.230
In the film, Williams plays a Soviet musician
in the circus who defects during a visit to

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:27.410
Bloomingdale's in New York, which is doubly
interesting as Nightcrawler also performed

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:31.400
in the circus before he met the X-Men.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:36.170
Prior to Scott's mall trip, he was at the
X-Mansion with his brother Alex, aka Havok.

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:40.650
And just before Alex left with Charles to
visit Moira at the CIA, the on-screen brothers

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.290
filmed a farewell scene.

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:45.930
This would have been the last moment that
Cyclops shared with his brother Havok as it

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:52.470
was while Cyclops was returning from the mall
that Havok died during the X-Mansion explosion.

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:56.660
Bryan Singer's mentioned that Michael Fassbender
filmed a beautiful scene outdoors which brought

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.370
tears to the filmmakers' eyes.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:03.150
From what Singer has said, it sounds like
the scene was of Magneto with his Polish family.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:07.580
According to Singer, although the scene was
incredible, it just didn't fit in the overall

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.710
story.

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:14.310
In the movie, Apocalypse has four Horsemen:
Storm, Angel, Psylocke and Magneto, but in

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:18.790
an earlier version of the script, Apocalypse
only had Storm, Angel and Magneto as his three

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:22.860
Horsemen and there were no plans at all to
include Psylocke in the movie.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:27.260
The initial script had Charles being kidnapped
by Apocalypse with the intention of counting

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:29.190
him as the fourth Horseman.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:32.750
But Kinberg and Singer realised that this
wouldn't really work, so they looked through

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.380
the comic book history of the various Horsemen
and "thought [that Psylocke] was the most

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:37.380
intriguing."

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:41.900
The filmmakers had actually just met with
Olivia Munn to talk about a part in Deadpool,

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:45.470
and it was when they came across some fan
art of her as Psylocke that they thought she

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.650
would be perfect for the role.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:52.310
Olivia Munn's role in the movie changed again
even after she was cast.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:56.040
Initially, it was announced that she'd be
playing Betsy Braddock, who in her comic book

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:58.560
origin story grows up in the UK.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:02.460
Olivia Munn is a huge fan of Psylocke and
the character's comic book history, however

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:06.810
the filmmakers decided that the movie would
not explore Betsy's life before she became

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:11.590
Psylocke for example, her time as a pilot
or a model, and she wouldn't have a British

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:14.820
accent either.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:18.820
Wolverine's cameo could have turned out quite
differently and there were many versions that

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:22.010
were considered, including not having him
in the film at all!

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:26.090
Another option the filmmakers looked at was
having Wolverine appear in the middle of the

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:30.100
movie, at which point he would have taken
on a team leader role to the young X-Men.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:35.080
However, this route was rejected as it interfered
with Raven's story-arc and other variations

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:36.590
didn't seem to work either.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:41.740
The final cameo during which we see Wolverine
go full-on beserker mode at the Alkali Lake

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:46.510
Weapon X facility turned out well, even if
the filmmakers haven't yet addressed the plot

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:50.990
hole of how he ended up there after Mystique,
disguised as Stryker, pulled him out of the

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:53.110
river at the end of Days of Future Past.

